# CBT Master — Complete Backend Reference

Stack: **Node.js 24 LTS + Express 5 + TypeScript + Prisma 8 + Supabase (Auth + Postgres)**
Payments: **Paystack**
Last verified against package registries: **August 2026**

---

## 1. Stack Justification (brief — this is already decided)

| Concern | Why this stack |
|---|---|
| Performance | Express 5 + Node 24 is more than sufficient for a CBT app's request volume (short-lived JSON requests, not compute-heavy). |
| Scalability | Supabase Postgres scales vertically first (fine for years), and your Express layer is stateless — horizontally scalable behind any load balancer. |
| Security | Supabase Auth offloads password storage, token issuance, and OTP flows to a security team whose full-time job this is, instead of you hand-rolling it. |
| Dev experience | You already know JS/TS from Flutter/Vue work — no new language. Prisma gives type-safe queries and migrations. |
| DB compatibility | Supabase *is* Postgres — Prisma talks to it exactly like any Postgres instance. |
| Long-term maintainability | Prisma schema + migrations is the single source of truth for your data model, versioned in git. |

**Alternative considered and rejected:** Using Supabase's auto-generated REST/GraphQL API directly from Flutter (no Express layer at all). Rejected because your CBT state machine (Step 6 below) needs server-side business logic — timer enforcement, idempotent submission, score computation — that a thin auto-generated CRUD API cannot safely enforce. Express is your business-logic layer; Supabase is your data + identity layer.

