## 11. Security Checklist

- [ ] `helmet()` applied globally for secure headers
- [ ] `cors()` restricted to your Flutter app's actual origin(s)/scheme, not `*`
- [ ] `express-rate-limit` on `/auth/*` and `/webhooks/*` routes specifically
- [ ] All input validated with Zod before touching the database (blocks malformed/oversized payloads)
- [ ] Prisma parameterizes all queries automatically — no raw SQL string concatenation, ever
- [ ] Paystack webhook signature verified on every call, using the raw body
- [ ] `service_role` Supabase key stored only in Express env vars, never sent to Flutter or committed to git
- [ ] Generic error messages sent to clients (`"Invalid credentials"`, not raw DB error text) — log full details server-side only
- [ ] RLS enabled on every Supabase table as a defense-in-depth layer even though Express uses the service key
- [ ] `.env` in `.gitignore`; secrets injected via your host's environment variable settings in production

